(* fs-records-b2s bound K_r = 3 in the fail-stop form (E21): three
   attacker-scheduled receive attempts of each installed Server peer, where
   a failed open of a parsed frame ends the worker instead of continuing
   with the entry state.  A parse failure and a rejected old target still
   continue.  Every trace of this form is a trace of fs-records-b2s-kr3.pvl.
   Conversely, a failed open of fs-records-b2s-kr3.pvl keeps the exact entry
   state, outputs nothing and emits only FsReceiveRejected, so deleting it
   from a trace leaves a trace of this form with every other event: a query
   that does not mention FsReceiveRejected and holds here holds there too
   (the deletion argument E21 of the records guide).  Used only for C2 and
   for C4 with adversary-chosen plaintexts. *)
expand FS_B2S_RECV_STEP(FsB2sRecv3, FsB2sRecvStop, FsB2sRecvStop).
expand FS_B2S_RECV_STEP(FsB2sRecv2, FsB2sRecv3, FsB2sRecvStop).
expand FS_B2S_RECV_STEP(FsB2sRecv1, FsB2sRecv2, FsB2sRecvStop).
